  "releaseNotes": "NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.ArbitrumOASIS v2.0.5\n\nConnects the OASIS to Arbitrum -- Ethereum's most popular optimistic rollup L2, with EVM equivalence, ~10x cheaper transactions, and full Ethereum security via fraud proofs. Stores OASIS holons, avatars, and NFTs on Arbitrum One or Nova. Part of the OASIS HOT-Swappable Provider Architecture. Ecosystem: https://oasisomniverse.one\n\nWhat's new since v2.0.4\n- Add native Arbitrum public balance CQL with fixed official RPC path (dd827e4)\n- Add runnable Arbitrum public balance CQL walkthrough and guide (1631f05)\n- Enroll Arbitrum read profile and verify native Mongo HTTP federation (ab1ca31)\n- fix(evm): cancel owned status HTTP requests per operation (87426f6)\n- fix(hyperdrive): preflight mode transitions against legacy-only providers (c316824)\n- fix(tests): keep L2 unit fixtures off public RPC and document Arbitrum privacy gap (8853856)\n- Organize HyperDrive provider working reports under dedicated WIP folder (b699b48)\n- security: remove a committed testnet chain private key (and a block-explorer API key) from provider DNA files, test harness configs and .env; the Arbitrum test harness reads OASIS_TEST_CHAIN_PRIVATE_KEY instead. The key is still in git history: rotate it. (fefa98c)\n- Share canonical finalized EVM transaction status across priority providers (7eb5a8c)\n- test(arbitrum): verify real encrypted wrapper with shared V2 policy fixture (368a16f)\n\nFull changelog\nhttps://github.com/NextGenSoftwareUK/OASIS/commits/master/Providers/Blockchain/NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.ArbitrumOASIS",
